## Architecture Rules (CRITICAL)

### Entrypoints are the unit of work

Every extension surface is a file or folder in `entrypoints/`. WXT generates `manifest.json`
from them — **never hand-write `manifest.json`**. Declare manifest fields in `wxt.config.ts`.

| Surface | Entrypoint | Export |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Background (service worker) | `entrypoints/background.ts` | `defineBackground(() => {})` |
| Content script | `entrypoints/*.content.ts` | `defineContentScript({ matches, main(ctx) })` |
| Popup | `entrypoints/popup/index.html` | framework app mounted in `main.{{ variables.ui_ext }}` |
| Options | `entrypoints/options/index.html` | framework app |
| Side panel | `entrypoints/sidepanel/index.html` | framework app |

### Always use the unified `browser` API

{% raw %}
```typescript
// CORRECT — works on Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari
import { browser } from 'wxt/browser';
const tab = await browser.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true });

// WRONG — raw chrome.* global is Chromium-only and callback-based
chrome.tabs.query({ active: true }, (tabs) => { /* ... */ });
```
{% endraw %}

`wxt/browser` is the native browser object since WXT 0.20 (no `webextension-polyfill`;
types from `@types/chrome` via the `Browser` namespace). Raw `runtime.onMessage` listeners
must reply with `sendResponse` + `return true`, not a returned Promise. Import storage from
`wxt/utils/storage` and testing helpers from `wxt/testing/vitest-plugin` /
`wxt/testing/fake-browser` (the old `wxt/storage` / `wxt/testing` paths are gone).

### Background service worker is event-driven

In Manifest V3 the background is a service worker that is **killed when idle**. Never store
state in module-level variables expecting it to survive. Persist with `wxt/utils/storage`; schedule
work with `browser.alarms`, never `setTimeout`/`setInterval` for anything long-lived.

{% raw %}
```typescript
// entrypoints/background.ts
import { browser } from 'wxt/browser';
import { onMessage } from '@/utils/messaging';

export default defineBackground(() => {
  browser.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(({ reason }) => {
    if (reason === 'install') {
      // first-run setup
    }
  });

  onMessage('getTabInfo', async ({ sender }) => {
    return { id: sender.tab?.id, url: sender.tab?.url };
  });
});
```
{% endraw %}

### Content scripts use `ctx` for lifecycle

The `ctx` (ContentScriptContext) cancels timers/listeners when the script is invalidated
(SPA navigation, extension reload). Never use bare `setInterval` or `addEventListener`.

{% raw %}
```typescript
// entrypoints/example.content.ts
export default defineContentScript({
  matches: ['*://*.example.com/*'],
  runAt: 'document_idle',
  main(ctx) {
    ctx.setInterval(() => console.log('alive'), 1000); // auto-cancelled on invalidation

    ctx.addEventListener(window, 'wxt:locationchange', () => {
      // handle SPA route changes
    });
  },
});
```
{% endraw %}

### Typed messaging only

Define one protocol in `utils/messaging.ts` and use `sendMessage` / `onMessage` everywhere.
Validate `sender` for any privileged action.

{% raw %}
```typescript
// utils/messaging.ts
import { defineExtensionMessaging } from '@webext-core/messaging';

interface ProtocolMap {
  getTabInfo(): { id?: number; url?: string };
  saveItem(data: { title: string }): { ok: boolean };
}

export const { sendMessage, onMessage } = defineExtensionMessaging<ProtocolMap>();
```
{% endraw %}

### Typed, reactive storage

{% raw %}
```typescript
// utils/storage.ts
import { storage } from 'wxt/utils/storage';

export const settings = storage.defineItem<{ theme: 'light' | 'dark' }>('local:settings', {
  fallback: { theme: 'light' },
  version: 1,
});

// usage
const current = await settings.getValue();
await settings.setValue({ theme: 'dark' });
const unwatch = settings.watch((next) => console.log(next));
```
{% endraw %}

## Permissions Rules

- Declare `permissions` and `host_permissions` in `wxt.config.ts`'s `manifest` block.
- Practice **least privilege** — prefer `activeTab` + `scripting` over broad `host_permissions`.
- Use `optional_permissions` + `browser.permissions.request()` for rarely-used capabilities.
- After changing permissions, run `npm run compile` so the generated manifest is rebuilt.

## Cross-Browser Rules

- Branch on build-time env, not user-agent sniffing:

{% raw %}
```typescript
if (import.meta.env.FIREFOX) {
  // Firefox-only path
}
if (import.meta.env.MANIFEST_VERSION === 3) {
  // MV3 path
}
```
{% endraw %}

- Per-browser manifest tweaks use the `manifest` function form in `wxt.config.ts`.
- Build other targets with `npm run build -- -b firefox` / `wxt build -b edge`.

## Build & Ship Pipeline

This project is scaffolded with real tooling — use it, don't reinvent it:

- **`wxt.config.ts`** — single source of truth for manifest, permissions, modules.
- **`package.json` scripts** — `npm run dev` (HMR), `npm run build`, `npm run zip`
  (store-ready zips, incl. Firefox sources), `npm run compile` (typecheck).
- See `.claude/patterns/cross-browser.md` and `.claude/patterns/publishing.md` for store submission.

